skibidi main {
    🚽 A matching numbered case must win even when `based` (default) is
    🚽 declared before it in source order. Regression for issue #179.
    rizz a = 2;
    ohio (a) {
        based:
            yapping("default A");
            bruh;
        sigma rule 1:
            yapping("A one");
            bruh;
        sigma rule 2:
            yapping("A two");
            bruh;
    }

    🚽 With `based` first and nothing matching, default must still fire --
    🚽 guards against over-correcting the fix.
    rizz b = 9;
    ohio (b) {
        based:
            yapping("default B");
            bruh;
        sigma rule 1:
            yapping("B one");
            bruh;
    }

    🚽 C-style fall-through *out of* `based`: nothing matches, so `based` runs,
    🚽 and with no trailing `bruh` it falls through into the following
    🚽 `sigma rule`. Locks in the fall-through semantics the fix changed most.
    rizz c = 9;
    ohio (c) {
        based:
            yapping("default C");
        sigma rule 1:
            yapping("C one");
            bruh;
    }
    bussin 0;
}
